atinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "hidus ancient place", "text": "lord shiva\"s big themple it is called pashupati nath .many many small temples are there .kailas parbat ,Bagmati river,also near by there. When people died his or her dead body is burning fire is in there .", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2018-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "CCFB8CF7179DBA18A85E4ECBA2203CDE", "name": "iconbir2046", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/iconbir2046", "username": "iconbir2046", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/de/e7/default-avatar-2020-37.jpg", "contribution_count": 3, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-10-12", "published_at_date": "2018-10-12"}, {"review_id": 624045762, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r624045762-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Beautiful but disturbing", "text": "Hindu Temple can not be enterd by non Hindu’s. Interesting complex with lost of dogs and apes. It becomes disturbing once you realise that you are an uninvited guest to someone’s cremation. Watching the ceremony is intriguing and cultural interesting, but also quite unpleasantly intimate and emotional. A religious gathering of Hindu’s with spectators on the side is a strange uneasy combination", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2018-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "88B4B23EE6DD295A399128EB77D1771C", "name": "Frank v", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/frankv787", "us