y active. When we visited and I presume everyday there were several cremations going on. It is a little shocking to western eyes. It was a glimpse into another culture that is memorable.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 3, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2018-09-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "640CE595A1FF1475E2E940CA2093D88A", "name": "travelsalot45", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/travelsalot45", "username": "travelsalot45", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/ed/00/default-avatar-2020-4.jpg", "contribution_count": 116, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2018-10-07", "published_at_date": "2018-10-07"}, {"review_id": 622774364, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r622774364-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Hindu Human Cremations & Respect Their Cultural Way", "text": "Arrived on Wednesday 04/07/18 with my driver & Tour Guide & admission fee NR1,000\nThis was certainly an experience in respecting the Hindu way in preforming Human Cremations & the Peshupatinath Temple area has been following traditions for hundreds of years.\nCertainly an unusual attraction for tourists keeping in mind we must at all times respect other cultures & what they believe in after death.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "solo", "stay_date": "2018-07-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "EB68D3D947A326BD6FCA2BA31AFC7D9F", "name": "STEPHEN N", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/uptonuponsevern", "username": "uptonuponsevern", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o